Parameter Meaning <code>from</code>, <code>to</code> <code>lat,lon</code> of each end; points more than 500 m from any road are rejected <code>at</code> Time of day, <code>HH:MM</code> (default <code>08:00</code>); served at the nearest quarter-hour <code>weekend</code> Use the weekend traffic curve <code>alternatives</code> Up to two extra routes, by the penalty method <code>avoid_charge</code> Add the quickest route that stays out of the Congestion Charge zone <p>The response is a GeoJSON <code>FeatureCollection</code>, quickest route first. Each feature carries <code>seconds</code>, <code>metres</code>, the <code>charge</code> it incurs at that time, and <code>learned_eta</code> (with <code>window_seconds</code>, the calibrated 10th to 90th percentile range) when the service was started with a model.</p> <pre><code>{
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "time": "08:15",
  "query_ms": 5.6,
  "features": [
    {
      "type": "Feature",
      "geometry": {"type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[-0.141, 51.5154], "..."]},
      "properties": {
        "name": "quickest",
        "seconds": 876.9,
        "metres": 3590.1,
        "charge": {"enters_zone": true, "charged": true, "amount_gbp": 18.0},
        "learned_eta": {"seconds": 1498.6, "window_seconds": [1206.8, 1568.5]}
      }
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre>
